1
00:00:00,734 --> 00:00:01,768
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

2
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:04,137
Please, Akira!

3
00:00:04,204 --> 00:00:06,406
I want to go so badly!

4
00:00:06,539 --> 00:00:07,974
Quit being so insistent.

5
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:10,510
This guy is a five-star chef!

6
00:00:10,577 --> 00:00:13,113
They serve meat that's out of this world.

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:15,348
I know this place.

8
00:00:15,415 --> 00:00:17,117
I heard it costs 100,000 yen per person.

9
00:00:17,183 --> 00:00:19,085
Please lend me the money!

10
00:00:19,152 --> 00:00:21,021
This will make my dream come true.

11
00:00:21,087 --> 00:00:22,422
No means no.

12
00:00:22,489 --> 00:00:25,025
You know I don't give advances
on your pay.

13
00:00:25,091 --> 00:00:26,259
Cheapskate!

14
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:30,864
Michiko, haven't you saved any money?

15
00:00:30,997 --> 00:00:32,132
No, I haven't.

16
00:00:32,232 --> 00:00:34,768
Ms. Daimon uses it on you-know-what.

17
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:36,836
If you want your dream to come true,

18
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,938
then try learning something from this guy.

19
00:00:39,139 --> 00:00:41,074
President Rokkakubashi of Hexagon Bridge?

20
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:45,712
His children's business did great,
and I heard he's worth 100 billion.

21
00:00:45,779 --> 00:00:48,715
- One hundred billion?
- Some people have got it all.

22
00:00:48,782 --> 00:00:52,352
Since President Rokkakubashi
also invested in Rat Coin,

23
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:56,289
I follow his social media
so I can learn from him.

24
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:58,458
And I've only got a few hundred yen.

25
00:00:59,426 --> 00:01:00,660
That's your own fault.

26
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:02,529
Oh, dear.

27
00:01:02,629 --> 00:01:05,498
It looks like I'll be getting
a few hundred points too.

28
00:01:05,832 --> 00:01:06,833
Mahjong!

29
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:10,236
Three closed triplets
with double <i>dora haneman.</i>

30
00:01:10,303 --> 00:01:11,971
- Really?
- Amazing!

31
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,340
- Too bad.
- Excuse me.

32
00:01:15,175 --> 00:01:16,409
Excuse me.

33
00:01:18,178 --> 00:01:19,412
Who are you?

34
00:01:20,046 --> 00:01:22,715
Can you check to see
if you can heal her illness?

35
00:01:23,183 --> 00:01:24,150
What?

36
00:01:24,617 --> 00:01:27,821
I'm sorry, but this isn't a hospital.

37
00:01:27,887 --> 00:01:30,156
We're only a doctor agency.

38
00:01:30,857 --> 00:01:32,125
I know that.

39
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:35,795
- Oh, my!
- Oh, dear!

40
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:37,931
You make dreams come true!

41
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:39,399
The guy worth 100 billion!

42
00:01:39,466 --> 00:01:41,701
This is the Famous Doctor Agency, right?

43
00:01:42,402 --> 00:01:44,971
I heard you have a doctor who will
operate no matter how difficult it is.

44
00:01:45,572 --> 00:01:47,140
Yes, we do.

45
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:50,410
Then I'd like that doctor
to operate on this girl.

46
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:54,347
If you need money, I'll pay for it.

47
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:56,983
No matter how much.

48
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:58,485
No matter how much?

49
00:01:58,751 --> 00:02:02,155
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

50
00:02:03,356 --> 00:02:06,426
Primary germ cell tumor
of the retroperitoneum.

51
00:02:06,493 --> 00:02:07,727
At another hospital,

52
00:02:07,894 --> 00:02:11,464
she was receiving radiation therapy
and chemotherapy,

53
00:02:11,831 --> 00:02:13,900
but they weren't having any effect,

54
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,936
and she was deemed inoperable.

55
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:21,307
After her mother posted
her condition on social media,

56
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:26,079
President Rokkakubashi here
indicated he would assist her.

57
00:02:26,379 --> 00:02:30,416
To have such a man of the day as
President Rokkakubashi visit us

58
00:02:30,517 --> 00:02:34,154
is certainly an honor, isn't it,
Assistant Director?

59
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:38,958
So this is the hospital
that you're restructuring, Mr. Tange?

60
00:02:39,025 --> 00:02:40,193
It's been a while.

61
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,096
You mean, you two know each other?

62
00:02:45,031 --> 00:02:47,066
The business world is a small one.

63
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:48,168
I see.

64
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:49,536
President Rokkakubashi,

65
00:02:50,236 --> 00:02:51,337
here you are.

66
00:02:52,772 --> 00:02:55,375
Would you autograph this for me?

67
00:02:55,475 --> 00:02:56,809
Certainly.

68
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:00,180
- Go ahead.
- Thank you.

69
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:02,015
There.

70
00:03:02,215 --> 00:03:03,449
Thank you.

71
00:03:03,550 --> 00:03:04,851
Isn't that great?

72
00:03:06,419 --> 00:03:08,821
I see it has metastasized to the lungs.

73
00:03:08,888 --> 00:03:12,625
The Next-Generation Director
who could do this is at a conference.

74
00:03:12,926 --> 00:03:16,529
But I'm the former director, and I'm here.

75
00:03:16,629 --> 00:03:21,167
No. This surgery is too difficult
for anyone except my Dr. Daimon.

76
00:03:21,401 --> 00:03:25,572
You mean this patient is being
referred to us

77
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:28,074
by Kanbara Famous Doctor Agency?

78
00:03:29,175 --> 00:03:31,277
This will be great PR for your hospital.

79
00:03:31,844 --> 00:03:33,980
I'm also thinking of paying
a separate reward.

80
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:35,381
A reward?

81
00:03:35,448 --> 00:03:37,217
A reward!

82
00:03:37,784 --> 00:03:42,188
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

83
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:46,192
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

84
00:03:46,659 --> 00:03:48,828
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

85
00:03:49,028 --> 00:03:51,731
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

86
00:03:52,098 --> 00:03:55,902
I'm amazed you're even using
a child's illness for publicity's sake.

87
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,438
It's publicity for me,

88
00:03:58,504 --> 00:03:59,939
the girl will be cured,

89
00:04:00,039 --> 00:04:01,341
and you will make money.

90
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:04,110
Good business is when
everyone wins, right?

91
00:04:04,177 --> 00:04:05,511
Exactly right.

92
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:11,417
Say cheese.

93
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:17,223
Is it okay if I post a photo?

94
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:18,992
Yes, it's okay.

95
00:04:19,058 --> 00:04:21,427
Thank you so much for what you're doing.

96
00:04:21,628 --> 00:04:23,263
When I'm cured,

97
00:04:23,997 --> 00:04:26,432
I'll practice even harder on the piano.

98
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:29,569
It's my dream to become a pianist.

99
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:31,571
Dreams are made to come true.

100
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:33,539
Do your best.

101
00:04:33,906 --> 00:04:35,308
Okay, we'll be going.

102
00:04:40,346 --> 00:04:43,249
Let's see. What's that girl's name again?

103
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:44,784
What?

104
00:04:45,151 --> 00:04:46,753
It's President Rokkakubashi!

105
00:04:46,819 --> 00:04:50,556
I can't believe you're here!
Can we get a photo together?

106
00:04:50,623 --> 00:04:53,726
- Certainly.
- Thank you! Okay, let's go.

107
00:04:53,893 --> 00:04:56,929
It must feel nice to spend money
to help other people.

108
00:04:57,797 --> 00:05:00,233
His type are the ones
who are the real winners.

109
00:05:00,466 --> 00:05:02,568
Tako, what would you do
if you had 100 billion?

110
00:05:02,735 --> 00:05:05,538
It's futile to talk about
hypothetical situations.

111
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:06,973
Can you get that, Mr. Kanie?

112
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:10,043
Doctors used to be called "winners."

113
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:12,945
But nowadays, surgeons are probably

114
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:15,114
the biggest losers among doctors.

115
00:05:15,181 --> 00:05:18,117
Anyone who wonders about
things like that is a loser.

116
00:05:18,184 --> 00:05:19,719
You are unexpectedly frank.

117
00:05:20,019 --> 00:05:20,853
Sorry.

118
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:29,929
Hello.

119
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:33,299
We met at the agency
the other day, didn't we?

120
00:05:35,134 --> 00:05:36,336
Thank you.

121
00:05:41,607 --> 00:05:44,377
I appreciate you operating on that girl.

122
00:05:45,044 --> 00:05:46,312
- Are you having lunch now?
- Yes.

123
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:48,781
Then I'll pay for it.

124
00:05:49,716 --> 00:05:50,783
You can't do that.

125
00:05:51,384 --> 00:05:54,253
Everyone! Have whatever you like!

126
00:05:54,587 --> 00:05:56,556
I'll pay for it.

127
00:05:57,490 --> 00:06:01,728
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance maverick doctor,
who was never part of</i>

128
00:06:02,061 --> 00:06:06,065
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

129
00:06:06,132 --> 00:06:08,401
- It's free!
- Ms. Daimon!

130
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:09,769
She sure is fast.

131
00:06:09,869 --> 00:06:11,904
Extra-large, since it's free!

132
00:06:12,071 --> 00:06:13,806
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

133
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:18,478
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

134
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:21,948
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

135
00:06:22,148 --> 00:06:23,383
<i>are her weapons.</i>

136
00:06:25,985 --> 00:06:27,086
Goodbye.

137
00:06:29,956 --> 00:06:30,957
Thank you for this meal.

138
00:06:31,023 --> 00:06:33,025
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

139
00:06:33,459 --> 00:06:35,862
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

140
00:06:35,928 --> 00:06:37,196
It's free!

141
00:07:01,621 --> 00:07:03,389
Ablating tumor. Pediatric Kelly clamp.

142
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,492
"People say it's a publicity stunt,

143
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:08,861
but all I want to do is

144
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:12,432
help those in need
and help a child achieve her dream."

145
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,268
That President Rokkakubashi
sure puts on a show.

146
00:07:15,835 --> 00:07:17,637
- Give me that back.
- Sorry.

147
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:22,608
But he's helping kids,
so I think it's pretty admirable.

148
00:07:22,708 --> 00:07:26,078
If he truly had good intentions,
would he write that? No.

149
00:07:26,913 --> 00:07:28,214
You wouldn't advertise it.

150
00:07:28,915 --> 00:07:30,183
It's just a publicity stunt.

151
00:07:30,917 --> 00:07:32,018
- Yes?
- Excuse me.

152
00:07:34,587 --> 00:07:36,222
Oh, President Rokkakubashi.

153
00:07:36,589 --> 00:07:38,224
I heard I could observe.

154
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,992
Please, have a seat.

155
00:07:43,896 --> 00:07:45,198
- Excuse me.
- Excuse me.

156
00:07:45,398 --> 00:07:48,701
As former director,
I'll explain the surgery.

157
00:07:49,168 --> 00:07:51,938
Mutsumi needs two surgeries. She needs

158
00:07:52,038 --> 00:07:55,107
retroperitoneum tumor removal
and inferior lobe excision.

159
00:07:55,174 --> 00:07:56,976
To reduce the burden on the patient,

160
00:07:57,076 --> 00:08:00,546
the operations will be performed
twice on separate days.

161
00:08:00,713 --> 00:08:01,981
Please, observe.

162
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:10,056
SURGERY TIME

163
00:08:13,226 --> 00:08:15,394
- Closing. 4-0 absorbable suture.
- Okay.

164
00:08:15,728 --> 00:08:17,997
That's fast.
Less than half the predicted time.

165
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:19,198
Well done, Daimon.

166
00:08:19,265 --> 00:08:20,967
As usual, you never fail.

167
00:08:24,804 --> 00:08:28,908
- Vitals?
- BP, 104 over 68. Pulse, 86, sinus.

168
00:08:28,975 --> 00:08:31,611
- Okay. Right decubitus position.
- What?

169
00:08:31,911 --> 00:08:33,546
We'll do the lung excision now.

170
00:08:33,746 --> 00:08:34,847
What?

171
00:08:35,147 --> 00:08:37,016
- What?
- Hold on here.

172
00:08:37,416 --> 00:08:39,185
We're only doing
the retroperitoneum today.

173
00:08:39,385 --> 00:08:41,621
If we do the lung,
we need differential lung ventilation.

174
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:44,624
Then fill her lungs with blocker,
then we can keep operating.

175
00:08:45,157 --> 00:08:46,459
Don't be ridiculous.

176
00:08:46,559 --> 00:08:49,195
If we operate on her longer,
it will be too much for her--

177
00:08:49,262 --> 00:08:51,731
Finishing it all at once is
less of a burden.

178
00:08:51,831 --> 00:08:53,699
Don't worry! I'm fast.

179
00:08:54,233 --> 00:08:56,903
- What are you waiting for? Move her!
- Right.

180
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:59,105
Prep the equipment to hold her in place.

181
00:08:59,171 --> 00:09:00,840
- Disinfect too.
- Right.

182
00:09:02,208 --> 00:09:04,377
- Get me a broncho and blocker.
- Right.

183
00:09:11,584 --> 00:09:13,319
The theater of the demon has begun.

184
00:09:13,886 --> 00:09:16,088
She's quite a character. Sorry.

185
00:09:16,289 --> 00:09:18,457
But she's very skilled. It will be fine.

186
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:29,669
- Short Satinsky clamp.
- Here.

187
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:32,705
- Hold her bronchus.
- Right.

188
00:09:34,273 --> 00:09:35,875
- You're too slow.
- Sorry.

189
00:09:38,511 --> 00:09:39,912
Let the oxygen flow.

190
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:43,950
Anesthetist, hurry up!

191
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:45,851
I know.

192
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:50,890
Poor Jonouchi has to deal with
this sudden change.

193
00:09:58,698 --> 00:09:59,699
Vitals?

194
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:03,102
BP, 104 over 69. Pulse, 80, sinus.

195
00:10:03,636 --> 00:10:05,705
- Done.
- Good work.

196
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:13,012
Well done, Daimon! Bravo!

197
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:14,981
I'm glad it worked out.

198
00:10:19,719 --> 00:10:20,953
Wait up!

199
00:10:21,487 --> 00:10:22,755
What is it?

200
00:10:22,822 --> 00:10:24,957
I've worked with you for a long time,

201
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:27,259
so I'm used to changes during surgery,

202
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,694
but today was unacceptable.

203
00:10:29,328 --> 00:10:31,631
But I never fail.

204
00:10:32,331 --> 00:10:34,467
Is it good enough if you never fail?

205
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:36,569
This patient was a child.

206
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:38,871
Think about how much a child can handle.

207
00:10:40,106 --> 00:10:41,273
Listen.

208
00:10:41,607 --> 00:10:44,844
I can't approve of that operation
you just did today.

209
00:10:45,344 --> 00:10:47,013
Why are you so seriously upset?

210
00:10:49,515 --> 00:10:51,250
Oh, all right.

211
00:10:51,350 --> 00:10:55,388
Tonight, I'll treat you to dinner.

212
00:10:56,455 --> 00:10:58,057
Ta-da!

213
00:10:58,157 --> 00:11:01,694
You get one free beef bowl
when you buy two!

214
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:04,630
I don't want it.

215
00:11:05,264 --> 00:11:06,399
Really?

216
00:11:06,799 --> 00:11:08,367
It's my treat, you know.

217
00:11:09,735 --> 00:11:11,103
Goodbye.

218
00:11:13,305 --> 00:11:14,573
Hey!

219
00:11:14,974 --> 00:11:16,308
It's extra-large too!

220
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:20,513
It's an extra-large size!

221
00:11:26,218 --> 00:11:27,953
Thank you for the surgery.

222
00:11:28,621 --> 00:11:31,023
Mutsumi is still sleeping.

223
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:34,226
Actually, it's you who I want to talk to,
Dr. Jonouchi.

224
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:37,730
Are you free later?

225
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:39,065
What?

226
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:46,138
Enjoy.

227
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:49,475
Let's toast to the successful surgery.

228
00:11:50,276 --> 00:11:51,677
Thank you.

229
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:02,188
This place is popular now
for making meals that fulfill dreams.

230
00:12:02,621 --> 00:12:04,390
I had to demand a reservation here.

231
00:12:04,623 --> 00:12:06,859
Why did you invite me?

232
00:12:07,593 --> 00:12:11,697
You seemed a little depressed.
I thought you could use a diversion.

233
00:12:13,532 --> 00:12:15,968
I had a little argument.

234
00:12:16,635 --> 00:12:19,538
- With your boyfriend?
- No, not that.

235
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,407
How can I describe her?

236
00:12:22,108 --> 00:12:23,909
My business partner.

237
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:25,611
I envy you.

238
00:12:26,078 --> 00:12:28,614
I've always worked alone
since I was young.

239
00:12:31,550 --> 00:12:35,187
I read in your book
that your life began with

240
00:12:35,387 --> 00:12:36,756
a 500-yen coin.

241
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:40,192
In high school,
my dad's company went bankrupt.

242
00:12:41,627 --> 00:12:43,863
After that, I lived a miserably poor life.

243
00:12:44,697 --> 00:12:46,632
My mother gave me a 500-yen coin and said,

244
00:12:47,466 --> 00:12:49,368
"This is everything we have right now."

245
00:12:50,236 --> 00:12:51,971
She had me hold it in my hand.

246
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:56,609
My dream was to eventually turn that into

247
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,845
five hundred million
and even five billion.

248
00:13:03,349 --> 00:13:05,785
So I guess you fulfilled that dream.

249
00:13:06,185 --> 00:13:08,187
I believe in the power of money.

250
00:13:09,255 --> 00:13:11,157
With money, you can go into space

251
00:13:11,624 --> 00:13:12,858
and fulfill any dream.

252
00:13:14,026 --> 00:13:15,494
I don't care if people say

253
00:13:15,594 --> 00:13:17,730
they're publicity stunts
or that I'm buying lives.

254
00:13:19,899 --> 00:13:22,368
Buying lives?

255
00:13:24,570 --> 00:13:25,805
Here you are.

256
00:13:29,909 --> 00:13:31,744
Okay, let's eat, shall we?

257
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:33,779
- Thank you for this meal.
- Thank you for this meal.

258
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:39,218
This is delicious.

259
00:13:42,188 --> 00:13:45,057
I see. Hiromi turned you down, did she?

260
00:13:46,659 --> 00:13:50,462
Poor thing. She doesn't get to eat
this delicious beef bowl.

261
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:52,998
Look at this.

262
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:55,067
It's President Rokkakubashi.

263
00:13:55,801 --> 00:13:59,371
Well...
What a lavish dinner he's having again.

264
00:13:59,905 --> 00:14:01,340
It says one meal is one million yen.

265
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:03,108
A million yen?

266
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:04,343
Really?

267
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:08,647
Hey! It's that place with the dream meat
I wanted to go to!

268
00:14:09,982 --> 00:14:11,217
What?

269
00:14:13,986 --> 00:14:15,487
- There she is!
- Hey!

270
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,190
Hiromi's on a date with
President Rokkakubashi?

271
00:14:18,257 --> 00:14:20,626
She got dream meat worth
one million all for herself?

272
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:26,198
That ticks me off! Akira, I want you
to ban her for life from tomorrow!

273
00:14:29,635 --> 00:14:30,903
This is delicious!

274
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:34,607
Really? Your daughter
wants to be a ballerina?

275
00:14:35,507 --> 00:14:37,176
That's her dream.

276
00:14:37,476 --> 00:14:40,279
But who knows whether
she'll achieve it or not?

277
00:14:40,346 --> 00:14:42,581
Dreams are made to come true.

278
00:14:43,749 --> 00:14:45,918
Is there any way I can help?

279
00:14:47,119 --> 00:14:48,020
What?

280
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,022
You can't stay at
that Famous Doctor Agency.

281
00:14:50,422 --> 00:14:54,660
I can get you into
a better paying hospital and surgeries.

282
00:14:55,628 --> 00:14:57,496
There's no reason for you to do that.

283
00:14:57,930 --> 00:14:59,164
I have my reasons.

284
00:15:00,499 --> 00:15:01,567
What?

285
00:15:09,475 --> 00:15:10,609
Mr. Rokkakubashi!

286
00:15:10,709 --> 00:15:12,511
Mr. Rokkakubashi, turn this way!

287
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:14,013
Let me lay you down.

288
00:15:25,090 --> 00:15:27,159
- Abdominal CT, immediately.
- Right.

289
00:15:27,359 --> 00:15:28,627
What's wrong, Jonouchi?

290
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:31,263
It's President Rokkakubashi!

291
00:15:37,336 --> 00:15:39,471
This is really pretty serious.

292
00:15:40,806 --> 00:15:42,107
- Director.
- Yes?

293
00:15:42,174 --> 00:15:45,577
If we operate successfully
on Mr. Rokkakubashi here,

294
00:15:46,211 --> 00:15:47,846
it will be great publicity.

295
00:15:47,913 --> 00:15:50,783
Publicity?
Don't speak of such vulgar things.

296
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:53,852
But I guess you're right.

297
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,154
Also,

298
00:15:55,754 --> 00:15:57,756
we could get a huge reward from him.

299
00:15:57,823 --> 00:16:02,394
Reward? I told you not to speak of
such vulgar things.

300
00:16:02,828 --> 00:16:06,598
- But I guess you're right.
- Right.

301
00:16:07,099 --> 00:16:10,736
So as your trusted subordinate,
I think I'm best suited to do it.

302
00:16:10,936 --> 00:16:13,072
- I'd really appreciate this chance.
- No way.

303
00:16:14,106 --> 00:16:15,341
You know,

304
00:16:15,541 --> 00:16:18,944
since I became a plebe, money is tight.
Give me a chance.

305
00:16:19,611 --> 00:16:21,380
Money's tight since you became a plebe?

306
00:16:22,181 --> 00:16:25,317
You will need an operation
in the near future.

307
00:16:26,418 --> 00:16:27,619
What is

308
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:30,022
wrong with me?

309
00:16:33,258 --> 00:16:34,460
Excuse me.

310
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:36,996
Doctor, tell me...

311
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:40,099
What's wrong with me?

312
00:16:40,399 --> 00:16:42,067
Hepatoma, stage three.

313
00:16:42,634 --> 00:16:44,737
There's a 12-centimeter tumor
in your right lobe.

314
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:47,306
- Ms. Daimon...
- Hepatoma?

315
00:16:49,541 --> 00:16:50,609
You're kidding.

316
00:16:50,709 --> 00:16:52,144
Let me operate.

317
00:16:52,211 --> 00:16:53,379
I'm good.

318
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:54,980
Ms. Daimon, hold on a second.

319
00:16:55,547 --> 00:16:58,617
You've been banned for life.
I have nothing to talk to you about.

320
00:16:59,351 --> 00:17:00,552
What's that all about?

321
00:17:00,619 --> 00:17:02,421
I don't need to speak to

322
00:17:03,255 --> 00:17:06,692
a woman who eats million-yen-beef
all for herself!

323
00:17:08,994 --> 00:17:10,062
Excuse me!

324
00:17:11,296 --> 00:17:12,598
- Daimon.
- What?

325
00:17:12,898 --> 00:17:14,566
- Stay away from this patient.
- Why?

326
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:15,667
Just stay away!

327
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:17,169
Allow me to introduce myself.

328
00:17:17,436 --> 00:17:19,171
I'm Former Director Ebina Takashi.

329
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:23,342
The director wants me to operate
on you, President Rokkakubashi.

330
00:17:23,409 --> 00:17:24,376
- You?
- Yes.

331
00:17:24,476 --> 00:17:26,211
- You will die!
- Daimon!

332
00:17:27,112 --> 00:17:28,113
Sorry.

333
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,649
Will Dr. Jonouchi

334
00:17:31,583 --> 00:17:33,385
be the anesthetist?

335
00:17:35,621 --> 00:17:37,890
If that's your request, she can be.

336
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:40,225
Jonouchi and I have worked together
many times.

337
00:17:40,459 --> 00:17:42,494
I want Dr. Jonouchi's opinion.

338
00:17:44,096 --> 00:17:46,999
Who do you think should be the surgeon?

339
00:17:47,399 --> 00:17:48,500
What?

340
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,606
The surgeon is...

341
00:18:00,012 --> 00:18:02,347
Dr. Ebina. If you would, please.

342
00:18:02,714 --> 00:18:03,849
What?

343
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,984
- Jonouchi...
- Okay.

344
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,253
Dr. Jonouchi,

345
00:18:09,188 --> 00:18:10,756
swear that I'll be cured.

346
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:13,959
- I will.
- Yes, sir!

347
00:18:16,995 --> 00:18:19,465
<i>There's no benefit to allowing
Dr. Ebina operate.</i>

348
00:18:19,798 --> 00:18:21,567
The world will be watching this surgery.

349
00:18:22,034 --> 00:18:24,670
Please allow me to operate
under the AI's guidance.

350
00:18:27,506 --> 00:18:30,175
There's nothing wrong with
letting Dr. Ebina operate.

351
00:18:30,476 --> 00:18:31,977
- But--
- Samejima.

352
00:18:32,077 --> 00:18:33,145
Yes?

353
00:18:33,846 --> 00:18:35,747
Here are the Hexagon Bridge documents.

354
00:18:36,081 --> 00:18:36,915
What?

355
00:18:37,182 --> 00:18:40,752
This details their stock trends
and the value of the company.

356
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,123
HEXAGON BRIDGE
CORPORATE RESEARCH REPORT

357
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,895
The patient is Shota Rokkakubashi, age 37.

358
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:51,430
He has stage three hepatoma.

359
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:53,532
Due to the patient's earnest request,

360
00:18:53,732 --> 00:18:56,668
his case will be treated as top-secret,

361
00:18:56,735 --> 00:18:58,537
so no word of it is leaked.

362
00:18:59,171 --> 00:19:00,973
As you can see,

363
00:19:01,340 --> 00:19:04,409
there is a 12-centimeter tumor
in his right liver lobe.

364
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:06,612
How's the middle hepatic vein?

365
00:19:06,712 --> 00:19:09,114
It has deeply permeated
the middle hepatic vein.

366
00:19:09,181 --> 00:19:11,850
- I thought so.
- Operating in these circumstances,

367
00:19:11,950 --> 00:19:14,953
it will be difficult to keep
30 percent of the liver.

368
00:19:15,387 --> 00:19:18,357
- Dr. Ebina, can you do this?
- What do you mean?

369
00:19:18,590 --> 00:19:19,424
Well...

370
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:23,529
What's more, Mr. Rokkakubashi
has a D- blood type.

371
00:19:23,862 --> 00:19:28,066
Only one in 200,000 people have
that rare blood type.

372
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,436
Therefore, we can't use
ordinary blood products.

373
00:19:32,337 --> 00:19:35,307
For this operation,
we'll use the patient's own blood.

374
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:37,342
It will be an autotransfusion surgery.

375
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,478
Autotransfusion.

376
00:19:39,545 --> 00:19:42,948
We'll need to transfuse about 600cc
of blood in this operation,

377
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:45,817
so we'll draw Mr. Rokkakubashi's blood

378
00:19:45,918 --> 00:19:47,886
three times before the surgery.

379
00:19:47,986 --> 00:19:49,154
So we'll store his blood.

380
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:52,057
We can draw for storage only once a week,

381
00:19:52,157 --> 00:19:53,992
so the surgery will be in about a month.

382
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,195
- Magnificent!
- Objection!

383
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:57,896
What now, Daimon?

384
00:19:57,996 --> 00:20:00,632
What if the surgeon messes up
and the patient bleeds more?

385
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:02,968
600cc of blood won't be enough.

386
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:07,673
- Well...
- Hey, are you saying I'll mess up?

387
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:10,475
You look more frightening than usual.

388
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:11,543
Quit making fun of me!

389
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:13,145
Not that long ago,

390
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:15,480
I was the director of
Lake Mashu Satellite Hospital 39!

391
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:16,748
So what about it?

392
00:20:16,848 --> 00:20:19,651
Dr. Ebina and I are preparing
for this surgery.

393
00:20:19,851 --> 00:20:22,187
If I don't do it, the patient will die.

394
00:20:22,254 --> 00:20:23,655
Butt out!

395
00:20:26,158 --> 00:20:27,960
I'm thinking about the patient.

396
00:20:29,628 --> 00:20:32,531
This time, the anesthetist will
control the surgery.

397
00:20:34,032 --> 00:20:35,467
No matter how good you are,

398
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:38,303
we can't let a rampaging surgeon
do this operation.

399
00:20:38,837 --> 00:20:40,138
Did something happen between them?

400
00:20:40,239 --> 00:20:42,074
I don't know.
I've never seen Dr. Jonouchi this way.

401
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,542
Jonouchi, calm down.

402
00:20:43,609 --> 00:20:46,578
I won't let you do this operation,
Ms. Daimon.

403
00:20:46,678 --> 00:20:49,982
Daimon, let's consider having you
as my assistant.

404
00:20:50,215 --> 00:20:51,383
In fact, be my assistant.

405
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:54,052
I wouldn't do it even if I were asked to.

406
00:20:54,152 --> 00:20:56,488
"I won't let you." "I won't do it."
What's with you two?

407
00:20:56,555 --> 00:20:58,257
- What's the matter?
- This is frightening!

408
00:20:58,357 --> 00:20:59,658
Daimon! Be my assistant!

409
00:21:11,136 --> 00:21:12,804
Once all this blood is used up,

410
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:15,407
you'll have to end the surgery, right?

411
00:21:16,141 --> 00:21:17,409
Don't worry.

412
00:21:17,509 --> 00:21:19,845
We'll have plenty for the surgery.

413
00:21:21,346 --> 00:21:23,415
I've got more money than I can use.

414
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:26,652
Who would have thought
I would need to save blood?

415
00:21:28,387 --> 00:21:30,489
Don't work too hard.

416
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:35,460
People think I spend extravagantly
and just play around,

417
00:21:35,861 --> 00:21:37,729
but the company can't do anything
without me.

418
00:21:39,831 --> 00:21:43,735
I envy you for having a talented
business partner, Dr. Jonouchi.

419
00:21:44,936 --> 00:21:46,138
Partner?

420
00:21:46,238 --> 00:21:47,806
- Dr. Ebina, right?
- What?

421
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:49,741
Well...

422
00:21:50,509 --> 00:21:52,377
- Excuse me!
- What's wrong?

423
00:21:53,378 --> 00:21:54,579
I'm sorry!

424
00:21:55,347 --> 00:21:56,214
News about

425
00:21:56,515 --> 00:21:59,418
- your illness has leaked.
- Really?

426
00:22:00,385 --> 00:22:03,388
President Rokkakubashi has
stage three cancer?

427
00:22:03,789 --> 00:22:06,024
"This will undeniably affect
Hexagon Bridge

428
00:22:06,091 --> 00:22:08,727
and possibly cause great worry
for their clients."

429
00:22:09,227 --> 00:22:12,331
There's been a complaint from
President Rokkakubashi.

430
00:22:13,098 --> 00:22:17,302
He wonders if this hospital
can protect its patients' privacy.

431
00:22:18,303 --> 00:22:20,238
We don't know where the leak came from,

432
00:22:20,305 --> 00:22:22,507
but I explained to President Rokkakubashi

433
00:22:22,574 --> 00:22:24,543
that our hospital is not to blame.

434
00:22:24,609 --> 00:22:26,411
This is a compliance issue
for the hospital!

435
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:27,846
Now...

436
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:31,650
I'll admit,
this is a regrettable situation.

437
00:22:31,983 --> 00:22:34,486
Why don't we wait and see
how it turns out?

438
00:22:34,820 --> 00:22:35,854
Wait and see?

439
00:22:35,954 --> 00:22:38,824
If the former director of surgery, Ebina,

440
00:22:39,458 --> 00:22:41,893
performs a successful surgery,

441
00:22:42,194 --> 00:22:45,997
I'm sure President Rokkakubashi
will feel a lot better about it.

442
00:22:46,064 --> 00:22:47,165
However,

443
00:22:47,232 --> 00:22:50,035
if something unforeseen happens,
heads will roll!

444
00:22:52,738 --> 00:22:54,239
- Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

445
00:22:54,940 --> 00:22:56,341
You understand what I mean, right?

446
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,622
- Ebina.
- Yes?

447
00:23:10,822 --> 00:23:13,959
Why do you look like
a frightened little pug?

448
00:23:14,259 --> 00:23:15,861
- Sorry.
- You know,

449
00:23:16,161 --> 00:23:18,063
I asked you to be the surgeon,

450
00:23:18,163 --> 00:23:20,432
but I didn't say you could do the surgery.

451
00:23:20,499 --> 00:23:21,466
What?

452
00:23:21,633 --> 00:23:28,607
Offer a huge sum to that incredible
surgeon, Michiko Daimon. Double it.

453
00:23:28,707 --> 00:23:30,709
Well, actually,

454
00:23:31,276 --> 00:23:34,613
- Daimon says she won't operate.
- She won't?

455
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:35,914
- Right.
- How come?

456
00:23:35,981 --> 00:23:40,218
Daimon and the anesthetist,
Jonouchi, had a falling out.

457
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:42,087
Don't worry about that.

458
00:23:42,788 --> 00:23:46,258
Michiko Daimon loves operating
more than having three meals a day.

459
00:23:46,691 --> 00:23:49,094
She'll do it for sure.

460
00:23:49,194 --> 00:23:51,229
- Just calm down.
- Yes, sir.

461
00:23:51,496 --> 00:23:52,631
Oh, dear.

462
00:23:53,832 --> 00:23:55,066
What will I do?

463
00:23:56,301 --> 00:23:57,469
What am I supposed to do?

464
00:23:58,837 --> 00:24:00,038
Jonouchi.

465
00:24:06,978 --> 00:24:09,614
Teamwork is important for this surgery.

466
00:24:09,714 --> 00:24:11,817
We need to support each other as partners.

467
00:24:14,486 --> 00:24:17,255
What? Is that all you want to talk about?

468
00:24:18,223 --> 00:24:20,258
I come here all the time now.

469
00:24:20,659 --> 00:24:23,528
The wine only costs one coin,
but it's pretty good. Drink up.

470
00:24:23,862 --> 00:24:25,230
- Thank you.
- Sure.

471
00:24:29,167 --> 00:24:31,536
Actually, about this surgery,

472
00:24:32,637 --> 00:24:35,073
don't you think we should include Daimon?

473
00:24:35,974 --> 00:24:37,476
Of course, I'll do my best.

474
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:41,947
Jonouchi, why did you choose me?

475
00:24:42,581 --> 00:24:44,616
I'm not so sure that I "choose" you.

476
00:24:45,617 --> 00:24:47,219
Probably because I felt sure about you.

477
00:24:48,253 --> 00:24:49,488
You felt sure about me?

478
00:24:50,856 --> 00:24:51,957
What do you mean?

479
00:24:52,023 --> 00:24:55,060
With Ms. Daimon doing it,
I would be very worried.

480
00:24:55,427 --> 00:24:56,828
I see.

481
00:24:57,796 --> 00:24:59,898
I see. All right.

482
00:25:01,032 --> 00:25:02,501
I'll be your partner!

483
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:04,836
- What?
- I'll make you feel secure.

484
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,471
Let's do our best together!

485
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:20,619
My wife gets angry when I drink too much.

486
00:25:20,719 --> 00:25:23,054
And when you dilute it,
you get double the amount.

487
00:25:23,154 --> 00:25:24,389
You dilute it?

488
00:25:24,556 --> 00:25:25,557
Dang, what a tightwad!

489
00:25:25,624 --> 00:25:27,058
It's my treat today.

490
00:25:27,492 --> 00:25:28,827
Order whatever you like.

491
00:25:30,662 --> 00:25:32,230
ALL ITEMS 100 YEN!
ONE-COIN MENU

492
00:25:32,430 --> 00:25:34,533
"One coin"? You mean one hundred yen?

493
00:25:34,633 --> 00:25:35,834
One hundred yen.

494
00:25:37,836 --> 00:25:39,170
I'll get drunk for sure.

495
00:25:42,807 --> 00:25:44,109
Oh, Hiromi.

496
00:25:44,576 --> 00:25:46,278
Why are you so late?

497
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:48,914
Well, something came up.

498
00:25:49,748 --> 00:25:52,851
You're drunk, aren't you? Are you okay?

499
00:25:54,185 --> 00:25:55,487
Where's Ms. Daimon?

500
00:25:55,787 --> 00:25:57,389
She already went to bed.

501
00:25:57,489 --> 00:26:00,625
She was upset
that you wouldn't let her operate.

502
00:26:04,162 --> 00:26:06,331
I wonder if I went too far.

503
00:26:06,531 --> 00:26:08,567
I think you both went too far.

504
00:26:09,434 --> 00:26:10,702
That Ms. Daimon...

505
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:14,139
Because she doesn't fail,
she keeps being unreasonable.

506
00:26:14,239 --> 00:26:15,307
You're right.

507
00:26:15,507 --> 00:26:19,511
But she's only unreasonable with
the people that she trusts.

508
00:26:21,846 --> 00:26:23,114
Oh, dear.

509
00:26:23,181 --> 00:26:25,550
Rat Coin has fallen again.

510
00:26:27,152 --> 00:26:28,386
Actually, Akira...

511
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:32,257
Cut the noise!
Don't you know what time it is?

512
00:26:32,557 --> 00:26:36,261
Hey, you. Don't you trust me?
How about it?

513
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:39,030
Breathe in.

514
00:26:40,465 --> 00:26:41,800
Breathe out.

515
00:26:44,569 --> 00:26:46,571
You can leave tomorrow just as planned.

516
00:26:47,172 --> 00:26:49,207
Mutsumi, isn't it great that
you can get out so soon?

517
00:26:51,910 --> 00:26:53,878
Dr. Daimon, thank you.

518
00:26:54,312 --> 00:26:55,547
No problem.

519
00:26:55,914 --> 00:26:57,349
- Actually...
- Yes?

520
00:26:59,117 --> 00:27:02,220
It looks like Hexagon Bridge is
in pretty serious trouble.

521
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,155
There's a ton of mudslinging going on.

522
00:27:04,422 --> 00:27:07,425
You know, I guess it isn't all
wine and roses for the rich.

523
00:27:07,759 --> 00:27:09,728
Social media is full of
negative comments too.

524
00:27:09,828 --> 00:27:12,631
How can people do this
to someone who's ill?

525
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,469
MONEY CAN'T BUY GOOD HEALTH, CAN IT? LOL

526
00:27:17,535 --> 00:27:19,704
HURRY UP AND RETIRE, ROKKAKUBASHI!

527
00:27:24,976 --> 00:27:26,811
She says she wants to talk to you.

528
00:27:28,179 --> 00:27:29,381
Go ahead.

529
00:27:34,753 --> 00:27:39,424
Mr. Rokkakubashi,
thank you for helping me.

530
00:27:44,729 --> 00:27:48,233
PLEASE USE THIS

531
00:27:59,577 --> 00:28:02,080
When Mutsumi heard about your situation,

532
00:28:02,414 --> 00:28:04,482
she said she wanted to help you this time,

533
00:28:04,549 --> 00:28:05,583
so she made that.

534
00:28:07,452 --> 00:28:10,488
What is your dream now, Mr. Rokkakubashi?

535
00:28:11,289 --> 00:28:12,357
What?

536
00:28:20,031 --> 00:28:21,800
I'd have to say, to live.

537
00:28:26,337 --> 00:28:28,740
Dreams are made to come true.

538
00:28:29,607 --> 00:28:30,875
Do your best.

539
00:28:35,113 --> 00:28:36,147
Mutsumi,

540
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:38,516
the breeze is cold,
so let's go back inside.

541
00:28:48,393 --> 00:28:50,195
Diseases were other people's problems.

542
00:28:54,632 --> 00:28:56,501
I thought if I paid enough money,

543
00:28:57,936 --> 00:29:00,705
I could change those kids' lives.
That's all I cared about.

544
00:29:03,708 --> 00:29:04,876
But

545
00:29:07,011 --> 00:29:09,614
I realized that some dreams
can't be bought with money.

546
00:29:12,183 --> 00:29:13,585
It will probably come true.

547
00:29:14,152 --> 00:29:15,386
What?

548
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:16,788
Your dream to live.

549
00:29:18,256 --> 00:29:20,058
The surgeon isn't that great,

550
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,460
but you've got an excellent anesthetist.

551
00:29:24,028 --> 00:29:25,330
I knew it.

552
00:29:25,563 --> 00:29:26,498
What?

553
00:29:27,398 --> 00:29:29,701
Dr. Jonouchi's business partner

554
00:29:30,468 --> 00:29:31,870
was you, wasn't it?

555
00:29:32,704 --> 00:29:33,872
What?

556
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:36,908
Dr. Jonouchi won't let you operate

557
00:29:37,575 --> 00:29:39,544
because you're too good for this.

558
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:42,747
I've experienced this before,
so I understand.

559
00:29:43,748 --> 00:29:46,985
Business partnerships aren't easy.

560
00:29:48,653 --> 00:29:50,488
We're not business partners.

561
00:29:51,256 --> 00:29:52,090
Really?

562
00:29:53,024 --> 00:29:56,461
To me, surgery isn't business.

563
00:29:56,861 --> 00:29:58,997
It's my hobby and specialty.

564
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:04,736
HATANOGAWA TABLE TENNIS CENTER

565
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:07,038
I feel sorry for President Rokkakubashi.

566
00:30:07,338 --> 00:30:10,842
I wonder who leaked the news
about his illness.

567
00:30:11,009 --> 00:30:13,144
Must be one of those operatives
for the tabloids.

568
00:30:13,912 --> 00:30:15,246
I wouldn't be so sure.

569
00:30:15,346 --> 00:30:17,048
People are attracted to
other's misfortune.

570
00:30:17,348 --> 00:30:20,618
People sense a business chance then!

571
00:30:20,718 --> 00:30:23,555
Who cares? I'm so bored!
I want to operate!

572
00:30:23,621 --> 00:30:26,558
- Oh, dear!
- Yes!

573
00:30:28,226 --> 00:30:30,161
Three more weeks until your surgery.

574
00:30:31,262 --> 00:30:33,198
- It hurts!
- Mr. Rokkakubashi!

575
00:30:33,631 --> 00:30:34,699
Are you okay?

576
00:30:34,966 --> 00:30:36,835
- What's the matter?
- He suddenly got worse!

577
00:30:36,901 --> 00:30:38,236
- Turn him face up.
- Okay.

578
00:30:40,338 --> 00:30:41,973
- It hurts!
- Abdominal guarding.

579
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:43,908
The tumor could be about to burst.

580
00:30:44,375 --> 00:30:45,910
Get Dr. Ebina! We operate now!

581
00:30:45,977 --> 00:30:47,145
Yes, ma'am!

582
00:30:48,413 --> 00:30:49,714
Mr. Rokkakubashi!

583
00:30:50,014 --> 00:30:51,182
Mr. Rokkakubashi!

584
00:30:52,617 --> 00:30:56,054
But we've only got one-third of
the blood we need.

585
00:30:56,154 --> 00:30:59,224
Yes. We need to keep hemorrhaging
to a minimum during surgery,

586
00:30:59,591 --> 00:31:01,626
- or we'll run out of blood.
- Really?

587
00:31:02,227 --> 00:31:03,461
Emergency surgery?

588
00:31:03,828 --> 00:31:04,929
Are you kidding?

589
00:31:05,496 --> 00:31:07,832
Michiko Daimon is on standby, right?

590
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:11,102
Nine. Ten. Eleven.

591
00:31:11,169 --> 00:31:12,804
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

592
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:14,272
PATIENT NAME
ROKKAKUBASHI SHOTA

593
00:31:18,943 --> 00:31:21,613
We will now conduct a right lobe excision.

594
00:31:21,713 --> 00:31:23,114
- Ready, sir.
- Ready, sir.

595
00:31:23,314 --> 00:31:25,316
- Ready. Scalpel.
- Here.

596
00:31:35,493 --> 00:31:36,728
- Monopolar.
- Here.

597
00:31:45,036 --> 00:31:47,038
I'll ablate the tumor
and middle hepatic vein.

598
00:31:47,639 --> 00:31:48,840
- Monopolar.
- Here.

599
00:31:49,507 --> 00:31:50,842
Here's where it gets difficult.

600
00:31:51,309 --> 00:31:53,144
Dr. Ebina, be very careful.

601
00:31:53,511 --> 00:31:54,579
I know.

602
00:31:56,481 --> 00:31:58,950
- Nineteen. Yes!
- Oh, no!

603
00:31:59,150 --> 00:32:00,418
Yes!

604
00:32:01,753 --> 00:32:03,488
- Sweat!
- Yes. Excuse me.

605
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:08,459
The adhesion is quite severe.

606
00:32:08,526 --> 00:32:10,295
Yes. It's very rigid.

607
00:32:11,896 --> 00:32:13,498
I'll ligate the vein branch.

608
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:14,732
- 3-0 silk.
- Here.

609
00:32:15,066 --> 00:32:16,434
- Got it. Kelly clamp.
- Here.

610
00:32:21,706 --> 00:32:22,807
Oh, darn!

611
00:32:23,908 --> 00:32:25,176
- Suction!
- Right.

612
00:32:25,843 --> 00:32:27,111
- Suctioning!
- Where did I cut?

613
00:32:27,312 --> 00:32:28,579
- Astriction! Gauze!
- Right!

614
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:30,648
Where is it? Where's the hemorrhaging?

615
00:32:31,316 --> 00:32:32,517
What was cut?

616
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:33,718
<i>Sweat!</i>

617
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:36,621
What the heck are you doing,
you idiot, Ebina?

618
00:32:36,821 --> 00:32:39,257
Ruri, where's Daimon?

619
00:32:39,324 --> 00:32:41,359
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

620
00:32:46,831 --> 00:32:49,701
I can't get through to
the Famous Doctor Agency manager either.

621
00:32:55,540 --> 00:32:57,575
Hemorrhaging has exceeded 400cc.

622
00:32:57,809 --> 00:32:59,077
BP falling.

623
00:32:59,277 --> 00:33:01,179
Stay calm, Dr. Ebina.
Stop the bleeding first.

624
00:33:01,279 --> 00:33:04,015
I know, but I can't find
where it's coming from.

625
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:09,420
Jonouchi, we better give him an infusion.

626
00:33:09,687 --> 00:33:11,222
If we use his blood now,

627
00:33:11,289 --> 00:33:13,157
- we could run out--
- I know that!

628
00:33:13,224 --> 00:33:15,093
We need to give him an infusion!
This is bad!

629
00:33:16,527 --> 00:33:17,729
Where the heck is it?

630
00:33:24,302 --> 00:33:25,503
PATIENT NAME
ROKKAKUBASHI SHOTA

631
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:32,076
Proceeding with the infusion.

632
00:33:36,347 --> 00:33:39,050
Good. Anyway, give me
the 4-0 monofilament.

633
00:33:40,318 --> 00:33:42,153
- Stop the hemorrhaging first.
- I know.

634
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:46,691
Hold on. Where the heck is
the hemorrhaging coming from?

635
00:33:49,227 --> 00:33:50,595
The D- infusion is on-going.

636
00:33:52,096 --> 00:33:53,831
What's your problem?
Stop the hemorrhaging now!

637
00:33:54,232 --> 00:33:56,534
Dr. Ebina!
Stop the hemorrhaging immediately!

638
00:33:56,801 --> 00:33:58,169
End the surgery!

639
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:00,471
End the surgery?

640
00:34:01,272 --> 00:34:03,007
At this rate, you'll never excise it.

641
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:05,109
It will cause us less harm

642
00:34:05,309 --> 00:34:07,345
to end the surgery instead of
letting him die during it!

643
00:34:11,849 --> 00:34:12,950
Harm?

644
00:34:14,352 --> 00:34:16,587
This patient's life depends on this.

645
00:34:17,822 --> 00:34:19,757
Who cares about any harm to you!

646
00:34:21,492 --> 00:34:22,660
Jonouchi.

647
00:34:22,727 --> 00:34:24,228
She's been possessed by Dr. Daimon.

648
00:34:24,429 --> 00:34:26,864
Dr. Ebina, there's only 50cc
of blood left! Stop the hemorrhaging now!

649
00:34:26,931 --> 00:34:28,032
I know.

650
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:30,301
What will I do?

651
00:34:31,436 --> 00:34:32,804
Jonouchi, what should I do?

652
00:34:44,048 --> 00:34:45,416
Change surgeons!

653
00:34:45,783 --> 00:34:47,018
Change?

654
00:34:47,218 --> 00:34:48,486
Who'll take over?

655
00:34:48,553 --> 00:34:49,754
You mean...

656
00:34:57,228 --> 00:34:58,529
- Ebina!
- Yes?

657
00:34:58,696 --> 00:35:02,900
Didn't I tell you to arrange
with Dr. Daimon to--

658
00:35:02,967 --> 00:35:03,935
Out of the way!

659
00:35:09,073 --> 00:35:10,741
- Dr. Daimon!
- Daimon!

660
00:35:10,842 --> 00:35:11,976
She's here!

661
00:35:12,076 --> 00:35:13,277
Don't close him up!

662
00:35:13,611 --> 00:35:14,846
We'll keep operating.

663
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:18,049
Michiko Daimon!

664
00:35:18,382 --> 00:35:19,817
- Do your best!
- Okay!

665
00:35:21,352 --> 00:35:22,620
I'm taking over, Kin.

666
00:35:23,488 --> 00:35:26,257
Dr. Daimon, there's no more blood.

667
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:37,335
- Remove his blood.
- What?

668
00:35:37,435 --> 00:35:39,504
Remove it? What will we do then?

669
00:35:39,704 --> 00:35:41,372
You want to kill the patient?

670
00:35:41,873 --> 00:35:43,007
Phlebotomy, right?

671
00:35:43,508 --> 00:35:44,509
That's right.

672
00:35:44,575 --> 00:35:46,944
Removing his blood
makes it easier to find the hemorrhaging.

673
00:35:47,745 --> 00:35:50,114
But if we remove any more,
he'll run out of blood.

674
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:59,390
With his current vitals,
we can remove 300cc.

675
00:35:59,624 --> 00:36:00,791
I'll phlebotomize now.

676
00:36:00,858 --> 00:36:02,627
Blood collection instruments
and dextran, now!

677
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:03,794
Right.

678
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,875
Removing his blood made his liver shrink.

679
00:36:18,609 --> 00:36:20,311
There's less hemorrhaging.

680
00:36:21,379 --> 00:36:22,547
I see it.

681
00:36:22,847 --> 00:36:24,682
I'll rebuild the vein. Drop my loupe.

682
00:36:24,749 --> 00:36:25,583
Right.

683
00:36:26,817 --> 00:36:28,553
- 6-0 monofilament.
- Here.

684
00:36:30,655 --> 00:36:33,024
- You, washing water.
- Right. Syringe.

685
00:36:33,090 --> 00:36:33,991
Here.

686
00:36:50,841 --> 00:36:52,009
Suturing complete.

687
00:36:52,109 --> 00:36:54,178
Hemorrhaging has stopped,
but there's no more blood.

688
00:36:54,278 --> 00:36:55,846
Can we continue the surgery?

689
00:36:55,947 --> 00:36:57,215
We have blood right here.

690
00:36:57,615 --> 00:36:59,317
You'll use the blood you just removed?

691
00:36:59,517 --> 00:37:01,619
But 300cc isn't nearly enough, Jonouchi.

692
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:03,487
If it's not enough, we'll dilute it.

693
00:37:03,754 --> 00:37:04,755
Dilute it?

694
00:37:04,956 --> 00:37:06,624
Diluted autotransfusion.

695
00:37:07,258 --> 00:37:09,227
- Lower my loupe.
- Diluted?

696
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:12,463
The removed blood is temporarily
replaced with fluid

697
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:14,465
to dilute the blood in the body.

698
00:37:15,032 --> 00:37:16,934
Doing so reduces the amount of blood

699
00:37:17,034 --> 00:37:19,237
needed to replace what's been lost.

700
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:23,407
However, he's already lost
more than double than predicted.

701
00:37:24,175 --> 00:37:27,578
If the anesthetist makes a mistake,
the patient could lose his life.

702
00:37:30,648 --> 00:37:33,951
I'll infuse 300cc of dextran
through the V-line for diluting.

703
00:37:34,385 --> 00:37:36,721
I'll isolate the base of
the middle hepatic vein. Satinsky clamp.

704
00:37:36,787 --> 00:37:37,622
Here.

705
00:37:37,688 --> 00:37:40,992
Daimon, even after diluting his blood,
he's still in danger.

706
00:37:42,059 --> 00:37:43,628
Shouldn't we replace his blood
and close him?

707
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,463
- I decline!
- I decline!

708
00:37:47,431 --> 00:37:49,900
Surgeon, keep hemorrhaging to a minimum

709
00:37:49,967 --> 00:37:51,269
and leave enough liver.

710
00:37:52,036 --> 00:37:53,337
That's pretty unreasonable.

711
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:54,939
You can't do it?

712
00:37:56,707 --> 00:37:58,142
I never fail.

713
00:38:00,144 --> 00:38:01,712
I'll keep ablating from the center.

714
00:38:01,779 --> 00:38:03,214
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

715
00:38:08,886 --> 00:38:10,354
It will be announced that

716
00:38:11,055 --> 00:38:12,857
President Rokkakubashi overcame
his cancer.

717
00:38:14,025 --> 00:38:17,295
Before that, we must buy.

718
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:19,730
Yes, sir.

719
00:38:20,731 --> 00:38:23,367
- Vitals?
- BP, 110 over 83.

720
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:25,503
Pulse, 80, sinus.

721
00:38:26,170 --> 00:38:27,338
Done.

722
00:38:28,739 --> 00:38:30,074
Thank goodness.

723
00:38:31,742 --> 00:38:32,743
SURGERY TIME

724
00:38:34,512 --> 00:38:36,547
Your dream came true.

725
00:38:39,517 --> 00:38:40,751
Ms. Daimon.

726
00:38:41,652 --> 00:38:42,753
Nice work.

727
00:38:45,056 --> 00:38:46,223
Same to you.

728
00:38:46,290 --> 00:38:47,658
Nice work.

729
00:39:04,375 --> 00:39:06,377
The surgery was a success.

730
00:39:08,312 --> 00:39:10,147
I believed that, with you there,

731
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:13,484
Dr. Jonouchi, it would be all right.

732
00:39:15,753 --> 00:39:17,755
I merely administered the anesthesia.

733
00:39:17,822 --> 00:39:21,459
My trustworthy partner
performed the surgery.

734
00:39:24,228 --> 00:39:25,830
How are you feeling?

735
00:39:26,230 --> 00:39:28,332
Let me know if there's anything you need.

736
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:35,172
I want you to be with me, Dr. Jonouchi.

737
00:39:36,474 --> 00:39:37,575
What?

738
00:39:38,743 --> 00:39:40,111
What if I told you that?

739
00:39:44,782 --> 00:39:45,983
I'm sorry.

740
00:39:46,751 --> 00:39:49,687
I do appreciate your feelings
for me though.

741
00:39:51,055 --> 00:39:55,025
I believe that my daughter will
fulfill her dream by herself.

742
00:39:56,861 --> 00:39:58,095
More than anything,

743
00:39:58,896 --> 00:40:00,164
more than security,

744
00:40:00,931 --> 00:40:02,266
and more than money,

745
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:07,938
I love that Famous Doctor Agency.

746
00:40:09,974 --> 00:40:11,075
I see.

747
00:40:16,013 --> 00:40:17,348
Excuse me.

748
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:18,449
Yes?

749
00:40:20,151 --> 00:40:21,385
- This is a melon.
- Right.

750
00:40:23,687 --> 00:40:28,392
Director Hiruma,
thank you so much for the phone call.

751
00:40:28,459 --> 00:40:30,661
We couldn't get through.

752
00:40:31,095 --> 00:40:33,030
It took years off my life!

753
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:35,633
- I am terribly sorry.
- It's okay.

754
00:40:36,267 --> 00:40:38,102
- Before I forget...
- Yes?

755
00:40:38,669 --> 00:40:39,837
Here is

756
00:40:40,704 --> 00:40:41,872
the usual bill.

757
00:40:41,939 --> 00:40:43,073
There it is.

758
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:46,710
PLEASE PAY THE FOLLOWING AMOUNT

759
00:40:46,777 --> 00:40:49,380
Isn't the number farthest to the left

760
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:52,249
usually a one or a two?

761
00:40:54,218 --> 00:40:57,788
Your trusted subordinate, Dr. Ebina,

762
00:40:58,389 --> 00:41:01,659
is the one who saved
President Rokkakubashi's life.

763
00:41:02,593 --> 00:41:07,264
I believe that this has been
publicity for your good name

764
00:41:07,698 --> 00:41:09,633
that's worth much more than that.

765
00:41:11,168 --> 00:41:12,636
That's exactly right.

766
00:41:13,871 --> 00:41:15,039
I accept

767
00:41:16,707 --> 00:41:18,342
your bill.

768
00:41:20,211 --> 00:41:24,114
I got it! Thirty million yen!

769
00:41:26,383 --> 00:41:28,519
Well...
If it isn't the assistant director?

770
00:41:28,953 --> 00:41:31,889
I greatly appreciate
the magnificent operation

771
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:33,557
by Dr. Daimon again.

772
00:41:33,757 --> 00:41:36,293
You don't appear to appreciate it.

773
00:41:37,528 --> 00:41:38,996
By the way, Assistant Director,

774
00:41:39,263 --> 00:41:41,799
do you have an idea

775
00:41:41,899 --> 00:41:44,068
who leaked news of
President Rokkakubashi's illness

776
00:41:44,134 --> 00:41:46,070
to the press?

777
00:41:47,238 --> 00:41:48,873
Why would I know?

778
00:41:49,273 --> 00:41:53,210
It's quite clear that
President Rokkakubashi's illness

779
00:41:53,310 --> 00:41:55,913
affected the running of his company.

780
00:41:56,647 --> 00:41:58,382
If you already knew that,

781
00:41:58,949 --> 00:42:03,687
you could take advantage of
the fall and rise of their stock

782
00:42:04,088 --> 00:42:06,757
and make money off of it.

783
00:42:08,759 --> 00:42:11,529
I cannot allow you to
make use of people's lives

784
00:42:12,296 --> 00:42:13,464
to improve your business.

785
00:42:13,797 --> 00:42:15,232
With all due respect,

786
00:42:16,166 --> 00:42:17,935
operating a hospital is

787
00:42:18,636 --> 00:42:20,437
a business that makes use of

788
00:42:21,872 --> 00:42:22,907
people's lives.

789
00:42:24,842 --> 00:42:26,110
Goodbye.

790
00:42:32,216 --> 00:42:35,119
Heaven forbid!

791
00:42:35,185 --> 00:42:37,421
Heaven forbid!

792
00:42:39,957 --> 00:42:41,158
How were our earnings?

793
00:42:41,425 --> 00:42:43,694
Before President Rokkakubashi's
illness became public,

794
00:42:43,894 --> 00:42:45,829
we short sold Hexagon Bridge shares

795
00:42:45,896 --> 00:42:48,399
and bought them back before
the announcement of the surgery.

796
00:42:48,799 --> 00:42:50,434
This is the profit we made.

797
00:42:50,935 --> 00:42:52,002
That's fairly reasonable.

798
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:53,037
HEXAGON BRIDGE

799
00:42:53,103 --> 00:42:54,939
With Dr. Ebina in charge of the surgery,

800
00:42:55,039 --> 00:42:57,675
what would you have done
if something had gone wrong?

801
00:43:00,544 --> 00:43:02,479
This company, without Rokkakubashi...

802
00:43:02,546 --> 00:43:03,581
HEXAGON BRIDGE

803
00:43:03,647 --> 00:43:04,882
...would have been easy to buy,

804
00:43:05,382 --> 00:43:07,751
and our profits would have been
even greater!

805
00:43:15,359 --> 00:43:17,328
Michiko Daimon!

806
00:43:27,738 --> 00:43:31,842
Oh, I see President Rokkakubashi
was released in good health.

807
00:43:32,743 --> 00:43:35,379
I wonder if he will pay a special reward.

808
00:43:35,479 --> 00:43:36,480
Really?

809
00:43:36,547 --> 00:43:39,350
- Then I'll get that dream beef!
- Me too.

810
00:43:39,416 --> 00:43:41,318
Not you! You already had some.

811
00:43:41,652 --> 00:43:43,621
Why can't I have it again?

812
00:43:43,821 --> 00:43:47,424
Sorry, but I don't think your dream
will come true, Michiko.

813
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:48,659
Really?

814
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:55,232
<i>This surgery made me realize
the importance of saving.</i>

815
00:43:56,166 --> 00:43:59,737
<i>I will reduce extravagances
and work to improve the business.</i>

816
00:44:00,037 --> 00:44:01,672
Really?

817
00:44:01,739 --> 00:44:03,173
It appears he realized

818
00:44:03,273 --> 00:44:05,976
the importance of saving
after giving his blood.

819
00:44:06,377 --> 00:44:11,382
Ms. Daimon, why don't you save
a little money as well?

820
00:44:12,116 --> 00:44:13,350
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

821
00:44:13,550 --> 00:44:16,487
<i>hates authority, and hates restrictions.</i>

822
00:44:17,421 --> 00:44:20,491
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

823
00:44:21,158 --> 00:44:22,459
<i>are her weapons.</i>

824
00:44:23,193 --> 00:44:25,396
Here goes! Yes!

825
00:44:33,070 --> 00:44:35,105
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

826
00:44:35,706 --> 00:44:38,642
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

827
00:44:42,312 --> 00:44:44,715
<i>There's a patient I want you to
perform a transplant for.</i>

828
00:44:44,782 --> 00:44:47,484
<i>- Okay, Nichotan!</i>
- Advanced hair replacement.

829
00:44:47,618 --> 00:44:48,919
<i>I'll work like my life depends on it.</i>

830
00:44:48,986 --> 00:44:50,988
We have to strike before we're struck.

831
00:44:51,221 --> 00:44:52,623
<i>Dr. Kaji, can you speak English?</i>

832
00:44:52,690 --> 00:44:54,058
<i>Is it okay to operate?</i>

833
00:44:54,158 --> 00:44:56,126
Don't operate on a patient like that.
